% =============================================================================
% dill — Governance ILL (TODO_0276): principal-indexed possession over gill
% =============================================================================
%
% Mechanization of THY_0045/THY_0046. The `poss` modality `says K A`
% ("K affirms / holds A") carries a principal index K; its ELIMINATION rule
% unifies the index (hypothesis principal = conclusion principal, dill.rules
% poss_l), so distinct principals cannot fuse — the partial-⊕
% no-cross-principal-collapse (THY_0045 Fact P1: "non-degeneracy is the shape of
% ⊕") realized as index unification, needing no residual predicate and no
% shared-engine change (a grade algebra's add/sub is only called in the forward
% `settle` path, never in backward cut, so a partial ⊕ stays calculus-local).
%
% ENCODING NOTES.
%  - This is the `says`/affirmation reading (monad(K,·), THY_0045 §5.4): no
%    linear zone restriction, hence no engine change. The real dill (P1/P2) uses
%    a dedicated `principal` sort with the partial-⊕ algebra and the Δ|_K
%    possession restriction.
%  - Principals are numeric identity tags carried on gill's `dist` grade sort:
%    distinct numerals = distinct principals. The dist ALGEBRA is never invoked
%    in backward cut; the only role of the index is UNIFICATION (poss_l) and the
%    fence `!le 0 K` (poss_r/poss_l), which is THY_0045's fence V ("well-sorted
%    principal terms") — it grounds K to a concrete principal so the rule cannot
%    fire with a freely-synthesized index (without it the refutations collapse).
%  - Surface is `says K A`, NOT `[K] A`: the `[...]` bracket collides with the
%    forward parser's array-literal lexer, so `[1] a` parses as app(arrlit,a).
%  - The inner weight-graded stake !_w A is modeled here by gill's graded comonad
%    !!_d A (an orthogonal graded modality), so the combined `says K (!!_d A)`
%    witnesses the orthogonal-composition cut (THY_0045 §5.3, Lemma O) through
%    the UNCHANGED generic cut.

@extends gill.

% Principal-indexed possession / affirmation: `says K A` = "held / affirmed by K".
% @category comonad = a graded modality with no special engine role (as gill's
% haul); the sticky elimination and no-cross-collapse live entirely in the rules.
poss: dist -> formula -> formula
  @ascii "says #1 #2"
  @prec 80
  @category comonad
  @polarity positive.
